WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
Troubleshooters'
Office

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.980
Someone talked you into it?!

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:07.480
Yes. After we left the dream, 
it started coming back to me.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.200
I think the pillow was 
given to me by someone.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:11.990
What?!

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.490
And just who was it?!

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.920
I can't remember it very clearly.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.990
I think it may have been a student.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.680
Do you think someone is 
trying to cause trouble?

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.000
Most likely.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.630
The way the shoe amasogi went berserk...

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.130
And the matter of the underpants amasogi...

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:32.890
It all seems a little too convenient 
to be simple malison disturbances.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.640
If someone were arranging them, 
it'd go a long way toward explaining it.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.140
But why would someone do that?

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.810
I have no answer to that, 
but we'll need to be on our guard.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.400
Aw, this is so, so, so boring!

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.400
Quiet down, Mimane.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.910
But things were just getting 
fun thanks to that pillow!

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.410
And then those two had to mess it up <i>again</i>!

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.730
Let's just kick their butts already!

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.900
Not happening. We promised 
not to do anything to them.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.570
What's up with you, Akito?!

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.800
Fine, then! I'll do it by myself!

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.050
Both of you, stop!

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.050
I apologize, Azami. 
I'll talk some sense into Mimane.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.560
Keep your promise.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.160
Or no more help.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.940
You're the ones short on time.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.940
Can we really trust her?

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.950
We still have no idea who 
she is or what she's after.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:40.450
She was the only clue that my 
fortune pointed us toward.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.950
I believe we should do as she says for now.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:47.080
No matter who she is, we need her help.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.460
Meh!

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.480
<i>That's right. This is all to obtain a shard.</i>

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.610
<i>If we can manage that, we'll be saved.</i>

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.680
<b>Tsukumogami and their masters.</b>

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:05.280
<b>A master is critical for a tsukumogami, 
to replenish their spent strength.</b>

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:29.040
<b>Tsugumomo</b>

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.110
<b>Tsugu</b>

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:40.540
m 0 0 l 0 -10 l 10 -10 l 10 0

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:40.540
m 0 0 l 0 -10 l 10 -10 l 10 0

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:40.540
<b>Chapter 6</b>

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:40.540
<b>The Lost Village</b>

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:39.920
"The Lost Village."

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.950
<b>Several Hundred Years Ago</b>

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.950
<b>Several Hundred Years Ago</b>

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.960
<i>At a certain house,</i>

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.950
<i>there were three tools that had been 
lovingly used for three generations.</i>

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:51.460
<i>At around the same time, 
they ascended, becoming tsukumogami.</i>

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:55.460
We tsukumogami want to be of use to you.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.610
Please, direct us as you see fit.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:02.470
But first, we have three wishes 
we would like you to agree to,

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:06.970
after which we will share our true names 
with you, and accept you as our master.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.100
Very well. What are they?

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:09.470
Right...

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.520
Since the three of us are sworn siblings,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.360
we ask that you allow us to stay together.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:23.040
And while we are tools, 
we do have personhood, as well,

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.370
and would like to be treated as such.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:30.550
Finally, there are limitations 
to the powers of tsukumogami,

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:33.330
so we ask that you do not demand 
more than is safe to provide.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.380
Very well.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:40.880
I welcome you all as guests in this house.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:46.180
<i>Arumi, the crystal ball, 
has the power to see the future,</i>

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.600
<i>but her predictions become less 
accurate the further she is,</i>

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.410
<i>in both time and distance, from the subject.</i>

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.340
<i>She was mostly used to gain insight into</i>

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.920
<i>the immediate future and to
 help make major decisions.</i>

00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.730
<i>As a pair of scissors,</i>

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.700
<i>I may not be a weapon, 
but I do have an edge.</i>

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.290
<i>That meant I was skilled in combat 
and used as a bodyguard.</i>

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:09.400
<i>And the one who saw the most use...</i>

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:13.140
<i>was Hifumi, a die that could manipulate fate.</i>

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:19.610
<i>Since her rolls could result in good luck, 
she served a far more critical role.</i>

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:25.090
<i>We were honored to see how much 
our master relied on Hifumi,</i>

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.430
<i>and were proud of her for it.</i>

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:31.180
You think I'm more amazing? 
What are you talking about?

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:34.460
Arumi can see the future 
and help avoid danger.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.190
Akito is strong enough to protect people.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:42.200
It's about who's right for the job, 
and we all serve our purpose well!

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.130
You two need more confidence!

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:50.140
As long as we're able to make people happy.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:59.560
<i>We lived peaceful lives, for a while.</i>

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.050
<i>But then...</i>

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.380
<i>After a while, strange monsters 
began to appear in the village.</i>

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:20.480
<i>And around the same time, 
Hifumi began to lose her strength.</i>

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.020
<i>Naturally, we had questions.</i>

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.480
My die...

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.840
It can manipulate fate based on the rolls,

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:32.990
but not always for the better.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.560
Should it roll a one, it brings 
misfortune to whomever rolls it...

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.250
And if you continue to roll in spite of that,

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:43.000
the misfortune accumulates into a curse...

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:46.510
One that turns people into monsters.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:52.420
<i>Our master had become obsessed 
with Hifumi's powers.</i>

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:58.810
<i>To ensure he would have only good luck, 
he would hire villagers to roll the die...</i>

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:03.410
<i>and have them continue 
until they became monsters.</i>

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:09.280
<i>She tried to stop him, but...</i>

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.660
And you don't care what 
becomes of the other two?

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:18.660
<i>And so she was forced into compliance.</i>

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:24.380
<i>We told the villagers the truth 
about what was happening.</i>

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:27.380
<i>We thought we were saving 
them, as well as Hifumi.</i>

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.380
<i>But...</i>

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:34.650
<i>It didn't work out that way.</i>

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:40.740
<i>The rage of the villagers showed no mercy 
to the tool that had been used against them.</i>

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.660
<i>Hifumi... All of us...</i>

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.540
<i>All we wanted was to be of use.</i>

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:11.420
<i>After leaving the village, we served 
several new masters, one after another.</i>

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:15.940
<i>But every time, they would 
inevitably disappoint us...</i>

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.290
<i>until, after fleeing our fourteenth master,</i>

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:23.810
<i>we lost all interest in 
serving anyone ever again.</i>

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:30.380
<i>A tsukumogami without a master 
loses their strength over time.</i>

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:36.700
<i>As we wandered, we began to 
sense our end approaching.</i>

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:04.520
<i>It was then...</i>

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.650
<i>that the door opened.</i>

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.080
Where are we?

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.410
Stop!

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:25.570
Who's there?!

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.500
We mean no harm! Please, lower your bow!

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:36.190
We wandered in here, 
following a strange red bowl!

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:38.080
If we aren't welcome, we will leave!

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:43.630
Arumi, I don't think he's willing to talk.

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:44.270
Right.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.400
Three. Four. Half.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.670
One. Seven. Half.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.290
Two. Five.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:56.530
Foresight? In that case...

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:57.450
He's using fire!

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.410
Two beats from now, a radius of ten jou!

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.960
Piercing Spirit Archery:

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:02.950
Blazing Red Arrow!

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:11.600
<i>We parried it?</i>

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.960
<i>But I don't know if I can do it again.</i>

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.560
<i>What do I do?!</i>

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:20.080
Wow! What was that, huh?!

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:23.430
So neat! Where are you from? 
What do you want?

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.900
What are these? Scissors?

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:27.660
Tell me about the outside!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.730
<b>Shared Fate, Shared Dream</b>

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:46.330
Nothing like a tsugumomo with a fine behind.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:54.880
So, I am the elder of this village, 
Tanmen the bowl tsukumogami.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.880
Everyone calls me Old Bowl.

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:02.900
<i>A tsukumogami's true form can give away 
a lot about their powers and weaknesses.</i>

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.960
<i>Is he trying to demonstrate 
that he means us no harm?</i>

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.250
It's nice to meet you. 
I'm Akito, a pair of scissors.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:12.170
I'm Arumi, the crystal ball.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:18.730
I'd like to welcome the two of 
you to Mayoiga, the lost village.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:23.530
I also apologize for the reception 
our guard, Yasuki, gave you.

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.280
Terribly sorry.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:29.420
There's a limit to the number of 
tsukumogami we can welcome here.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:35.800
And more than anything, we can't have the 
gods or their hounds finding our village.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:42.300
It's all right. But I'd like to 
know more about this place.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:45.520
Everyone here is a tsukumogami...

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:48.310
And I don't sense the presence of any humans.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.730
We were on the verge of losing all 
strength before arriving here,

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:56.310
but we're both feeling much better now.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.530
Where does this power come from?

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:00.820
A long time ago,

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:06.070
there was a house tsukumogami 
that had a grand black front gate.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:12.610
The terrible treatment our kind 
was receiving wounded his heart,

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:16.360
and he wished that tsukumogami 
could survive without humans.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:21.840
And thus, he became our 
paradise himself: our Mayoiga.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.390
This place can support all these 
tsukumogami without any humans?!

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:30.450
Unfortunately, I can't answer 
all your questions yet.

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:34.960
But rest assured, this place 
is a paradise for tsukumogami.

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:38.720
I imagine the two of you have become 
fed up with humans as well, yes?

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:43.240
You're welcome to remain here, as one of us.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:45.820
Thank you, sir.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:52.020
<i>After we arrived in Mayoiga, it wasn't 
long before we began to fit in.</i>

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.650
This sucks!

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:59.100
<i>Mimane, the mirror, was always 
looking for things to amuse her.</i>

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:02.080
Huh? And then? Eh?

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:03.260
<i>When we first arrived, she would buffet us 
with questions from morning to night.</i>

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.740
What? But why?

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:05.890
<i>Even Arumi and I grew tired of it.</i>

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:06.510
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.480
<i>Yasuki the bow was the exact opposite,</i>

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.340
<i>speaking only when necessary.</i>

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.040
I apologize for before.

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:21.020
Mimane starts to sulk about wanting to leave 
the village whenever newcomers appear.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:24.620
<i>That's</i> why you were shooting at us?

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:30.030
<i>He made a terrible first impression, 
but it seems he's really just overprotective.</i>

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.230
Not bad at all!

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:41.710
<i>Chikage, the spear, is said to be 
the fiercest warrior in Mayoiga.</i>

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:46.610
<i>Old Bowl trusts her implicitly, and she 
would often organize the other tsukumogami.</i>

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:44.660
Up for another round?

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:46.060
Yes, please.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.970
<i>With no domineering or greedy 
humans to be found,</i>

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.470
<i>Mayoiga really was a 
paradise for tsukumogami.</i>

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:57.480
<i>But it had its mysteries, as well.</i>

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:03.280
A bath like this, inside a house?

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.680
<i>What was the power that 
kept the village going?</i>

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:12.240
<i>Why did Old Bowl let us in after telling 
us there was a limit to the population?</i>

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:16.000
<i>And why were they hiding from the gods?</i>

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:20.160
<i>Even Mimane wouldn't offer any answers.</i>

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:24.140
Fitting in well, son?

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:26.180
Yes.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:28.100
That's good to hear.

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:33.940
Out of curiosity, have you known 
that Arumi girl for a while?

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:38.860
Yes, we're like siblings. We've known each 
other for as long as we can remember.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:40.770
I see.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:45.280
A very nice ass on that one.

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:51.410
<i>A great deal of time then passed.</i>

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:56.840
<i>We had started to consider the 
village our second birthplace.</i>

00:14:58.170 --> 00:14:59.920
<i>But one day...</i>

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:02.420
Everyone, come quickly!

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.170
It's Danjurou and Kirihime...

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:08.670
They've reverted to their original forms?

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.090
Lost their spiritual power.

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:13.220
I thought that couldn't happen here?

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:19.680
Arumi, Akito... I need to 
speak with the two of you.

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:23.080
Where are we?

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:24.850
The center of Mayoiga.

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:28.070
A hallway that leads to the cornerstone 
everything was built on.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:32.300
This is the tsukumogami 
of the lost village...

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.450
Miurahi-sama.

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.450
He's mummified?

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:42.960
How did he end up like this?

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:47.460
It began over a thousand years ago...

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:50.780
There was a volcanic eruption, 
and a resulting catastrophe.

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:53.180
As the people began to starve and suffer,

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:56.720
the tsukumogami that served 
them suffered from abuse...

00:15:56.720 --> 00:16:00.220
and many lost their power as a result.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:05.480
Miurahi-sama regretted this deeply, 
and appealed to the god of this region.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:10.690
He wished to create a place where 
tsukumogami on the verge of

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:13.990
passing away could rest, if only temporarily.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:17.740
But his wish fell upon deaf ears.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:23.270
The god whose duty was to look after 
that area shirked their responsibility.

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:26.380
And as he saw his fellows fall one by one,

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:31.380
Miurahi-sama gathered a chosen 
group of tsukumogami...

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:36.390
and slew the region's god.

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:39.140
That's why you all fear the gods...

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:41.540
But why kill one?

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.520
For a shard.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:48.520
Gods who are entrusted with a region to 
oversee carry a shard within themselves.

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:51.440
A fragment of the pillar, Ame-no-Mihashira.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:56.610
Crystallized malison, capable of dictating 
the nature of existence itself.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:17:01.050
Miurahi-sama embedded the 
shard within himself,

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:03.720
obtaining the very power of a god.

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:06.840
But the power was immense,

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:11.600
with even the slightest wavering thought 
growing into a maelstrom, given form.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:14.760
So Miurahi-sama decided to 
sever his own consciousness,

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.590
meditating on the sole purpose of

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:18.790
maintaining Mayoiga, 
until he was mummified.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:23.060
But that shard is on the verge 
of losing its strength...

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:28.820
Seeing this inevitability, 
Miurahi-sama had us seek out tsukumogami

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:30.750
who have grown tired of the ways of men.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:31.580
You mean...

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:32.570
Correct.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:38.240
In order to obtain another shard, 
we must once again slay a god.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:43.700
<i>I see. That definitely isn't the kind of 
thing you tell someone on their first day here.</i>

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:47.090
<i>Killing a god isn't a simple task.</i>

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:51.710
<i>Even if it succeeds, it means becoming 
the target of a divine vendetta.</i>

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:55.340
<i>Now that we know the truth, if we 
refuse, we'll probably be killed.</i>

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:57.720
<i>Could the two of us escape?</i>

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:01.720
<i>But that would mean more 
hardship for Arumi...</i>

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:06.850
<i>I don't want to lose anyone else.</i>

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:08.300
<i>Never again.</i>

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:16.530
I feel the same way, brother.

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:29.270
<i>As the limit of the shard's power 
drew near, our planning commenced</i>

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:32.930
<i>with the selection of the god 
who would be the best target.</i>

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:36.880
The god we killed before, Iwanagahime,

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:41.410
had grown weak after using 
her power to cope with a famine.

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:46.890
Regardless, facing her with 108 powerful 
tsukumogami still resulted in a battle

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:51.320
that lasted seven days and nights, 
with over a hundred casualties.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:54.970
As such, the gods still seek to punish us.

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:58.640
Which means we cannot afford to make 
any moves that will get us noticed.

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:00.680
Arumi.

00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:01.500
Right.

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:11.860
My power, High Foresight,

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:16.170
should be able to show us the path 
that leads to the future we desire.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:20.200
<i>Arumi's predictions can 
only be used once a month.</i>

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:23.930
<i>So, once a month, we had her take a look.</i>

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.190
<i>Every time, the crystal ball 
showed nothing but</i>

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:29.530
<i>the villagers of Mayoiga,
with nothing out of the ordinary.</i>

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:33.940
<i>Which meant that staying the current 
course would be for the best.</i>

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:38.450
<i>But more villagers lost their 
strength as time passed...</i>

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:43.320
Hey, woman! Are these predictions any good?!

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:46.650
It's been thirty years now, 
with nothing to show for it!

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:49.380
If the results are the same, 
that means we're doing the right thing.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:51.370
<i>Some of the tsukumogami demanded 
that we take immediate action.</i>

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:50.680
It's not time to act yet...

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:51.890
Don't be a fool!

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:55.840
<i>But not long after that, there was a 
change in the crystal ball's vision...</i>

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:58.140
What is that?

00:19:59.070 --> 00:20:01.850
<i>A black shape was revealed 
within the crystal ball.</i>

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:06.320
<i>And just as we had seen, we found it 
in a forest among the mountains.</i>

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:11.690
It'd be dangerous to approach.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.720
True enough, but someone's 
decided to scout ahead.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:16.360
Wow, what is this thing?!

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.020
Mimane!

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:26.730
<i>The black shape seemed to attack anyone 
who approached, almost defensively.</i>

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:32.620
<i>We attacked from every direction, 
and were able to capture it.</i>

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.450
Blood Mirror!

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:34.920
Gotcha!

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:41.130
And this is the lead that 
the fortune led us to?

00:20:55.350 --> 00:21:00.810
<i>The black obi tsukumogami who appeared 
before us said her name was Azami.</i>

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:05.280
<i>She didn't share much else about herself...</i>

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.940
<i>But the fortune turned out to be true.</i>

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:12.940
<i>She knew which regional god was at their 
weakest, and how to weaken them further.</i>

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:17.600
<i>She had the exact information 
our village needed.</i>

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:22.690
<i>So, with Azami's guidance, 
we headed toward that region.</i>

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.620
<i>That was where we encountered 
another Azami, who was waiting.</i>

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:32.460
<i>She gave us three conditions for her help.</i>

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.580
<i>We had to give rise to</i>

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:37.060
<i>supernatural aberrations that would 
drain the regional god's strength,</i>

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:40.730
<i>continue doing so until Azami said to stop...</i>

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:44.570
<i>and stay away from the malison exorcists.</i>

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:48.960
<i>We agreed to her conditions, 
and have been acting as she requested.</i>

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:53.330
We can't afford to lose Azami's help yet.

00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:54.960
Keep that in mind.

00:21:56.090 --> 00:21:57.330
Fine.

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:20.710
Hey! Sorry for the wait.

00:22:20.710 --> 00:22:21.860
It's okay.

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:24.850
But that new game hasn't been installed yet.

00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:26.070
Say what?!

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:27.320
Why in the—

00:24:00.860 --> 00:24:03.510
I can't believe Mayoiga 
even has a hot spring.

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:05.880
Impressive, huh?

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:20.310
Hey, hey! What exactly is 
your relationship with Akito?

00:24:20.530 --> 00:24:24.850
We're sworn siblings who were 
born in the same storehouse.

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:28.320
Sworn siblings? What is that? 
So you're not lovers?

00:24:28.580 --> 00:24:31.410
Lovers?! He and I would never...

00:24:31.410 --> 00:24:33.660
Huh? But why not?

00:24:35.420 --> 00:24:36.880
These are huge!

00:24:37.540 --> 00:24:39.380
And he never does this?

00:24:39.380 --> 00:24:40.450
He does not!

00:24:40.450 --> 00:24:42.460
Why not? They're so big!

00:24:42.460 --> 00:24:43.330
I don't know!

00:24:43.630 --> 00:24:47.240
Hey, you're different here, too! 
Let me see, come on!

00:24:47.240 --> 00:24:49.780
Wha... S-Stop!

00:24:50.090 --> 00:25:03.100
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:24:51.290 --> 00:24:54.730
A fighting game amasogi has 
appeared at the arcade?!

00:24:54.730 --> 00:24:58.390
And an even more terrifying 
threat awaits us at school!

